    bootstrap_reads_transiently_broken_shared_working_copy_2026-09-05, 1, "2026-11-03 stale check (conc): STILL LIVE, narrowed not closed. ROOT CAUSE: scripts/bootstrap/bootstrap-from-scratch.sh builds the live checkout (repo_root = PWD), never an isolated copy or commit; it has no git worktree add, git archive or src/** snapshot copy. Shared state: the live src/** files of one checkout, written by other sessions. Interleaving: session A starts a multi-hour stage; session B rewrites or restores a file (torn write or transient conflict markers); the stage parser reads it mid-write. Mitigations present: (1) conflict-marker preflight at about :826-840 (git grep line-initial markers in src/*.spl, exit 64) covers only markers present at start; (2) stage3 source-inputs before/after compare (:4805-4839) and seed_inputs fingerprint pre/post (:3683, :3720) fail CLOSED on drift, so no stale artifact is published, but the lane still aborts after hours. Policy: .spipe/policy/vcs.sdn:57 unique_workspace: required with main_worktree: read_only means sessions should not write the checkout a bootstrap reads, but that is convention, not enforced against the bootstrap input. Fix direction (not done here): run stages from a pinned snapshot (worktree at a sha, as handle_bootstrap already does with create_bootstrap_snapshot) and keep the drift check. Kept open."

